---
import Base from '../layouts/Base.astro';
import LegalPage from '../components/LegalPage.astro';

const toc = [
  { id: 'short-version', label: 'The short version' },
  { id: 'on-your-iphone', label: 'On your iPhone' },
  { id: 'on-your-mac',   label: 'On your Mac' },
  { id: 'cloud-engines', label: 'If you opt into cloud engines' },
  { id: 'website',       label: 'This website' },
  { id: 'contact',       label: 'Questions' },
];

const title = 'Privacy — rekody';
const description = 'rekody runs on your own device. No accounts, no telemetry, no servers. Your voice never reaches us.';
---

<Base title={title} description={description}>
  <LegalPage
    eyebrow="Privacy"
    title="Your voice stays on your device."
    updated="July 8, 2026"
    summary="rekody runs on your own device. There are no accounts, no telemetry, and no servers. We can't see your data because it never reaches us."
    toc={toc}
  >
    <section id="short-version">
      <h2>The short version</h2>
      <p>
        rekody turns your speech into text on the device in your hand. It has no sign-up, no analytics inside
        the app, and it never checks in with a license server. We don't run servers that could receive your
        audio, so your words have nowhere to go but into the app you're typing in.
      </p>
    </section>

    <section id="on-your-iphone">
      <h2>On your iPhone</h2>
      <p>
        The rekody keyboard app records only while you dictate, transcribes on the device with an on-device
        speech model, and places the finished text where your cursor is. <strong>Your audio never leaves your
        iPhone.</strong>
      </p>
      <ul>
        <li>The speech model is downloaded once and runs fully offline. No audio or transcript is ever uploaded.</li>
        <li>Your dictation history is a local file inside the app. It stays on your iPhone, and you can delete any entry, or all of them, at any time.</li>
        <li>There are no accounts, no sign-in, and no analytics or tracking. rekody asks for no personal information.</li>
      </ul>
      <h3>Why the keyboard asks for Full Access</h3>
      <p>
        iOS only lets a keyboard place text into another app once you turn on <strong>Allow Full Access</strong>.
        rekody uses it for exactly that, and for the small shared container that hands your finished words from
        the app to the keyboard. It does not use Full Access to send anything off your device, because rekody has
        no server to send it to.
      </p>
      <div class="callout">
        <p>
          rekody is off in password and other secure fields by design. It won't offer to dictate where iOS marks
          the input as secure.
        </p>
      </div>
    </section>

    <section id="on-your-mac">
      <h2>On your Mac</h2>
      <p>
        rekody for Mac is a free, MIT-licensed tool (<a href="https://github.com/rekody/rekody" target="_blank" rel="noopener noreferrer">github.com/rekody/rekody</a>).
        Audio capture, voice detection, transcription, cleanup, and typing the text at your cursor all happen on
        your device. With the default on-device engine, or the on-device Apple Intelligence cleanup,
        <strong>nothing leaves your machine</strong>.
      </p>
      <ul>
        <li>Your dictation history is a local file: <code>~/.config/rekody/history.json</code>. Delete it whenever you like.</li>
        <li>API keys you add are stored in the macOS Keychain, never in plaintext on disk.</li>
        <li>The only network call the app makes on its own is checking GitHub for new releases when you run <code>rekody update</code>.</li>
      </ul>
    </section>

    <section id="cloud-engines">
      <h2>If you opt into cloud engines</h2>
      <p>
        On Mac, you can optionally configure cloud speech-to-text or LLM providers (Deepgram, Groq, OpenAI,
        Anthropic, and others) using <strong>your own API keys</strong>. When you do, your audio or text goes
        directly from your Mac to that provider under their terms. There is no rekody server in the middle,
        because we don't run any. The iPhone app is on-device only and has no cloud engines.
      </p>
    </section>

    <section id="website">
      <h2>This website</h2>
      <p>
        rekody.com is a static site. It uses privacy-friendly, cookie-less analytics (Vercel Analytics) for
        anonymous page-view counts. No tracking cookies, no ad pixels, no fingerprinting.
      </p>
    </section>

    <section id="contact">
      <h2>Questions</h2>
      <p>
        Email <a href="mailto:hi@rekody.com">hi@rekody.com</a>, or open an issue on
        <a href="https://github.com/rekody/rekody" target="_blank" rel="noopener noreferrer">GitHub</a> for the Mac tool.
        For security reports, email <a href="mailto:security@rekody.com">security@rekody.com</a> or use a
        <a href="https://github.com/rekody/rekody/security/advisories/new" target="_blank" rel="noopener noreferrer">private security advisory</a>.
      </p>
    </section>
  </LegalPage>
</Base>
